{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_compression_hook", "label": "compression() per-actor hook", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Overrides the store-level default per actor class \u2014 none for tiny state, high-level zstd for large text-heavy state. Returning undefined falls back to the store default; the framework calls it on each persist.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/object-storage/per-actor-policies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_encryption_hook", "label": "encryption() per-actor hook", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "Lets PCI / HIPAA / GDPR-scoped data use a separate master key AND a separate HKDF context from non-sensitive data, so compromise of one keyring does not expose the other.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/object-storage/per-actor-policies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_integrity_hook", "label": "integrity() per-actor hook", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "The third hook alongside compression() and encryption(): signs the stored body with HMAC-SHA256 so tamper-in-place is detected at read, worthwhile even for data that is not secret. Configuring it makes the tag mandatory on read.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/object-storage/per-actor-policies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_self_describing_manifest_read", "label": "Reads follow the manifest, not the current override", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Decoding uses the self-describing ATS1 manifest carried in the body, so an object encrypted under pciKeyRing is decrypted via pciKeyRing whether or not the actor's current encryption() says so \u2014 rotating an actor's policy therefore does not break old data as long as the keys and algorithms are still available.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/object-storage/per-actor-policies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_only_object_storage_reads_hooks", "label": "Only the object-storage stores read these hooks", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Ten of the eleven snapshot stores and nine of the ten durable-state stores accept PersistenceOptions and never look at it (#960). On SQLite, Postgres, Cassandra, Mongo, DynamoDB and the in-memory reference store an integrity(), encryption() or compression() override buys nothing and raises no error \u2014 the directive is dropped on the floor. Verify the control against the store you actually run.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/object-storage/per-actor-policies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_uniform_keyring_across_cluster", "label": "Uniform encryption config across cluster nodes", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Actors must see the same encryption config on every node, or a sharded entity that migrates cannot be read where it lands. Pass key rings from the same source everywhere.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/object-storage/per-actor-policies.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_self_describing_manifest_read", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_compression_hook", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/object-storage/per-actor-policies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_only_object_storage_reads_hooks", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_integrity_hook", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/object-storage/per-actor-policies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_uniform_keyring_across_cluster", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_encryption_hook", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/object-storage/per-actor-policies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_compression_hook", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_compression_compressionconfig", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/object-storage/per-actor-policies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_encryption_hook", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_encryption_encryptionconfig", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/object-storage/per-actor-policies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_integrity_hook", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_encryption_body_integrity_hmac", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/object-storage/per-actor-policies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_per_actor_policies_only_object_storage_reads_hooks", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_object_storage_compression_compressionconfig", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/object-storage/per-actor-policies.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}